<%# Data table wrapper.

    Handles the parts that are easy to get wrong and easy to forget:
      - an accessible name, via <caption> visually hidden
      - horizontal scroll on narrow screens, in a focusable, labelled region so
        keyboard users can actually reach and scroll it (WCAG 2.1.1). A plain
        overflow div is not keyboard-scrollable without a tabindex.
      - the card surface, hairline dividers and hover states from tables.css

    Locals:
      caption - required. Describes the table for assistive tech.
      class   - extra classes on the wrapper

    Pass <thead>/<tbody> as a block. %>
<div class="table-container <%= local_assigns[:class] %>">
  <div class="table-wrapper">
    <div class="overflow-x-auto focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary"
         tabindex="0"
         role="region"
         aria-label="<%= caption %>">
      <table class="table-base">
        <caption class="sr-only"><%= caption %></caption>
        <%= yield %>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
